%% param_inspect_uninstantiated.glp — NEGATIVE guard, case (iii) of the
%% abstract-parameter routing matrix (parameterized-types.tex
%% sec:abstract-parameters; spec: docs/type system/typed-program.md "Modular
%% Checking via Abstract Parameters").
%%
%% pskip/1 INSPECTS its parameter: the element position holds the constant `done`,
%% a functor/constant at a parameter position.  By the conclusion of
%% lem:parametricity, an inspecting procedure is NOT parametrically well-typed and
%% takes the PER-INSTANTIATION route — it is not certified by the abstract route.
%%
%% Here pskip is never instantiated (no monomorphic caller pins X).  The
%% abstract-parameter route is the sole means of certifying a parametric procedure
%% outside a program, and an inspecting procedure acquires a well-typing only per
%% instantiation, so a checker presented with it and no instantiation has nothing
%% to certify.  Loaded standalone it is therefore REJECTED
%% (sec:abstract-parameters).  Within a program an instantiation supplies the
%% verdict; a callerless procedure there goes unchecked (typed-program.md "Programs
%% and Modules").
%%
%% Contrast with case (iv), min_polarity_bug3.glp: an inspecting procedure that IS
%% instantiated, where the per-instantiation check runs and (there) rejects.
%%
%% Run (from /Users/udi/Grassroots/GLP/glp_runtime/):
%%   printf 'load ../programs/tests/param_inspect_uninstantiated.glp\n:quit\n' | bin/glpc

procedure pskip(Stream(X)?).
pskip([done|Xs]) :- pskip(Xs?).
pskip([]).
